---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { buildPageTitle } from '../lib/seo';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={buildPageTitle('How We Research and Compare Products')}
  description="How AltPik selects products, compares trade-offs, checks prices, uses shopper feedback, and keeps affiliate recommendations independent."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <header>
      <p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-brand-700">Editorial standards</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900">How we research products</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
        AltPik publishes research-based shopping guides. Our goal is to explain which option fits a
        real use case, what it costs, and what you give up—not to call every popular product “the best.”
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="article-prose mt-12">
      <h2>What we compare</h2>
      <p>
        We start with the decision a shopper is trying to make. Depending on the category, we compare
        dimensions, materials, compatibility, capacity, included accessories, warranty information,
        recurring owner complaints, availability, and price-to-usefulness.
      </p>

      <h2>Where information comes from</h2>
      <p>
        Research uses manufacturer specifications, product manuals where available, retailer
        listings, and patterns in verified-purchase feedback. A high rating or bestseller label is
        never enough on its own. We look for repeated strengths and repeated failure points.
      </p>

      <h2>Hands-on testing and evidence</h2>
      <p>
        Most guides on AltPik are desk research, not hands-on or laboratory testing. We state direct
        experience only when it occurred and can be described. Product photos supplied by retailers
        illustrate the exact item; they are not presented as original test photography.
      </p>

      <h2>How picks are ranked</h2>
      <p>
        Rankings weigh fit for the article's use case, practical trade-offs, value, availability, and
        the consistency of owner feedback. “Editor's Pick” means the strongest overall fit for that
        guide. “Best Value” means a lower-cost option that preserves the functions most buyers need.
      </p>

      <h2>Prices and updates</h2>
      <p>
        Prices shown are snapshots and can change at any time. The updated date records a meaningful
        editorial or product check—not an automatic date refresh. Always confirm price, seller,
        shipping, compatibility, and return terms on the retailer's page.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate independence</h2>
      <p>
        AltPik participates in the Amazon Associates program and may earn from qualifying purchases.
        Affiliate status does not buy placement or change a product's rank. Sponsored placements are
        not mixed into editorial rankings. Affiliate links are clearly disclosed and marked for
        search engines.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Product details change. If you notice an incorrect specification, unavailable item, or broken
        link, email <a href="mailto:apiszczat2222@gmail.com">apiszczat2222@gmail.com</a>. We review
        concrete corrections and update the article when warranted.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
